  rerank input means the question was not reranked (the rerank input is the first max(rerank-candidates, topK) fused chunks), and an unreranked retrieval
  returns the fused order cut to topK, so position 1 is the named chunk. The reports' returnedPosition (not rendered by any check) agree: 1 for the named
  chunk, 2 to 7 or null for the others. The block's introducing line: "Questions whose matched chunk differs between the traced reference and the traced
